.TH NOSTR-HOMED-PROVISION 1 "2026-09-25" "nostr-homed 0.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nostr-homed-provision \- portable-home provisioning CLI (enroll / push / pull / verify / status)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nostr-homed-provision
.I subcommand
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nostr-homed-provision
is the user-facing operator CLI that mirrors the broker's PROVISION_HOME code
path. It generates a portable-home identity, publishes and reads back the
kind-30078 pointer, and drives the same snapshot / chunk / encrypt / batch /
publish pipeline that
.BR nostr-home-syncd (8)
runs in the background.
.PP
The tool is intentionally linked against the full porthome stack (libhanami +
libnostr + libcurl). It is a user-space operator tool, NOT a component of
.BR nostr-authd (8)
or
.BR pam_nostr (8) \(em
those daemons enforce a much narrower dependency closure. Use this tool from
a shell (or a provisioning ansible role), never from a PAM stack.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B enroll
Generate a fresh identity + wrap_seed + home_key stack; write a 0600
account file suitable for the seed-authority / broker seed drop. Optionally
publish the initial empty (gen 0) pointer to the configured relays.
.TP
.B status
Pretty-print, JSON-dump, or single-field query the
.I porthome-status.json
under a caller-selected home. Same schema as
.BR nostr-home-status (1),
scoped to any home (not just the caller's).
.TP
.B pull
Fork+exec
.BR nostr-home-fetch (1)
against a
.B --dest
staging directory. Mirrors the broker's semantics: SSRF-gated fetch, size
caps, network-timeout budget, exit codes forwarded verbatim from the helper.
.TP
.B push
Snapshot a home tree, encrypt + upload chunks to Blossom, publish a new
kind-30078 pointer. Reuses the same
.I nh_syncd_push_batch
implementation the daemon uses.
.B --dry-run
prints the manifest plan without touching any relay or Blossom server.
.TP
.B verify
Fetch the current pointer, decrypt the manifest, then HEAD-check every chunk
across the configured Blossom server list. Reports per-chunk replication
counts and returns 5 if any chunk falls below the requested threshold.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Each subcommand has its own option set; see the per-subcommand pages. Common
options that appear in most subcommands:
.TP
.B \-\-account\-file \fIPATH\fR
Read pubkey, home_key, relay list and Blossom server list from PATH (the
0600 file produced by
.B enroll\c
).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit machine-readable JSON on stdout instead of a text summary.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print planned actions; do not open any relay connection, do not write any
file outside the CLI's own stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-relay \fIwss://...\fR
Append a home relay. Repeatable. Also written back to the account file when
supplied alongside
.B --account-file
in
.BR push .
.TP
.B \-\-blossom \fIhttps://...\fR
Append a Blossom server. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-insecure
Permit http:// URLs and private/link-local Blossom hosts. Off by default;
the SSRF gate rejects those otherwise.
.TP
.B \-\-min\-replication \fIN\fR
(\fBpush\fR only.) Refuse the push if fewer than N Blossom servers hold every
chunk. Default 2. Exit code 77 on insufficient replication.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <out-dir>/<pubkey8>.account.json
0600 account file emitted by
.BR enroll .
Contains pubkey, secret, home_key, relay list, Blossom list, d-tag.
.TP
.I /run/nostr-auth/session/<uid>/home_seed
Broker seed drop path. Written by
.B enroll \-\-seed\-drop
(requires
.B --uid
and root). Consumed by
.BR nostr-home-syncd (8)
and
.BR nostr-home-fuse (8).
.TP
.I <home>/.local/state/nostr-homed/porthome-status.json
Status file read by
.B status
(and by
.BR nostr-home-status (1)).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_ENABLE_PORTHOME_EXPERIMENTAL
Must be set at build time; the CLI is gated behind this feature flag in
CMake. Runtime environment variables consumed by individual subcommands are
documented on their own pages.
.SH EXIT CODES
Exit codes are subcommand-specific; see the per-subcommand pages. Broadly:
.RS
.PP
0 success, 1 malformed input or field miss, 2 bad argument, 3 missing state
file, 5 chunk missing on verify, 65 SSRF gate rejection, 71 network failure,
72 manifest decode failure, 75 crypto failure, 76 internal error, 77
insufficient replication.
.RE
.SH SECURITY
The tool holds secret key material in memory. It sets
.B RLIMIT_CORE
to zero and calls
.BR mlock (2)
on secret buffers. Account files are written with mode 0600.
.B \-\-redact
replaces secret fields with \(dqREDACTED\(dq in stdout, useful for pasting
into tickets. Never log the account file contents; the pubkey is safe to
publish, everything else is not.
.SH EXAMPLES
Provision an identity and publish the initial pointer:
.PP
.RS
.nf
nostr-homed-provision enroll \\
    \-\-relay wss://relay.example \\
    \-\-blossom https://blossom.example \\
    \-\-out\-dir ~/.config/nostr-homed \\
    \-\-publish
.fi
.RE
.PP
Push the current home:
.PP
.RS
.nf
nostr-homed-provision push \\
    \-\-account\-file ~/.config/nostr-homed/abcd1234.account.json \\
    \-\-bump\-gen \-\-min\-replication 2
.fi
.RE
.PP
Verify replication and check current syncd state:
.PP
.RS
.nf
nostr-homed-provision verify \-\-account\-file ...account.json
nostr-home-status \-\-field syncd.state
.fi
.RE
